      "text": "The given series is an alternating series of consecutive odd numbers. We can observe that the series starts at 1 and increases by 3 each time, alternating between positive and negative terms.\n\nThe series can be written as:\n\\[ 1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55 \\]\n\nTo find the sum, we need to determine the number of terms in the series and then use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\nFirst, let's find the number of terms. The \\(n\\)-th term of the series can be written as \\(6n - 5\\). We need to find the value of \\(n\\) for which the \\(n\\)-th term is 55:\n\\[ 6n - 5 = 55 \\]\n\\[ 6n = 60 \\]\n\\[ n = 10 \\]\n\nSo, there are 10 terms in the series.\n\nNext, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series. The sum \\(S\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic series is given by:\n\\[ S = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l) \\]\nwhere \\(a\\) is the first term, \\(l\\) is the last term, and \\(n\\) is the number of terms.\n\nHere, \\(a = 1\\), \\(l = 55\\), and \\(n = 10\\). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[ S = \\frac{10}{2} (1 + 55) \\]\n\\[ S = 5 \\times 56 \\]\n\\[ S = 280 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is:\n\\[ \\boxed{280} \\]",
